# EduHub Email System Development Guide

## System Overview

The EduHub email system is **fully automated** using Hasura event triggers. No manual email sending from the frontend.

### Core Components

1. **[functions/callNodeFunction/sendEnrollmentEmail/index.js](mdc:functions/callNodeFunction/sendEnrollmentEmail/index.js)** - Sends emails on enrollment status changes
2. **[functions/callNodeFunction/sendSessionReminders/index.js](mdc:functions/callNodeFunction/sendSessionReminders/index.js)** - Sends reminders for FIRST sessions only
3. **[backend/metadata/databases/default/tables/public_CourseEnrollment.yaml](mdc:backend/metadata/databases/default/tables/public_CourseEnrollment.yaml)** - Event trigger configuration
4. **[backend/metadata/cron_triggers.yaml](mdc:backend/metadata/cron_triggers.yaml)** - Session reminder scheduling

## Email Function Development Rules

### Function Structure
```javascript
export default async function functionName(req, logger) {
  logger.info("########## Function Name ##########");
  
  try {
    // Input validation
    // GraphQL client setup
    // Business logic
    // Email template processing
    // Variable replacement
    // MailLog insertion
    
    return {
      success: true,
      messageKey: 'SUCCESS_KEY',
      // ... other response fields
    };
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error(`Error: ${error.message}`, { error });
    return {
      success: false,
      error: error.message,
      messageKey: 'ERROR_KEY'
    };
  }
}
```

### Status Mapping (sendEnrollmentEmail)
- `APPLIED` → `APPLICATION_RECEIVED` template
- `CONFIRMED` → `APPLICATION_CONFIRMED` template  
- `INVITED` → `INVITE` template
- `REJECTED` → `DECLINE` template
- `REGISTERED` → `REGISTRATION_CONFIRMED` template

### Session Reminders (sendSessionReminders)
- **CRITICAL**: Only send reminders for the FIRST session in each course
- Three reminder windows: 24h, 1h, 15m (with tolerance)
- Use MailLog metadata for duplicate prevention
- Filter: `sessionInWindow.id === firstSessionInCourse.id`

### Variable Replacement Patterns
```javascript
const replaceVariables = (text) => {
  return text
    .replaceAll('[User:Firstname]', user.firstName)
    .replaceAll('[User:LastName]', user.lastName)
    .replaceAll('[Enrollment:CourseId--Course:Name]', course.title)
    .replaceAll('[Enrollment:CourseLink]', `${FRONTEND_URL}/course/${courseId}`)
    .replaceAll('[Session:Title]', session.title)
    .replaceAll('[Session:StartDateTime]', sessionStart.toLocaleString())
    .replaceAll('[Session:Duration]', duration)
    .replaceAll('[Session:ReminderText]', reminderText);
};
```

## Testing Guidelines

### Test File Structure
```
functions/callNodeFunction/
├── functionName/
│   ├── __tests__/functionName.test.js
│   └── index.js
└── __tests__/
    ├── helpers/mockData.js
    └── integration.test.js
```

### Test Setup Pattern
```javascript
import { jest } from '@jest/globals';

const mockLogger = {
  info: jest.fn(),
  debug: jest.fn(),
  error: jest.fn(),
  warn: jest.fn()
};

describe('FunctionName', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    jest.clearAllMocks();
  });

  it('should load and be a function', async () => {
    const { default: functionName } = await import('../index.js');
    expect(typeof functionName).toBe('function');
  });
});
```

### Testing Commands
```bash
cd functions/callNodeFunction

# Run all tests
npm test

# Run with coverage  
npm run test:coverage

# Watch mode for development
npm run test:watch

# Run specific test
npm test -- --testNamePattern="should handle DELETE operations"
```

